Laura, if your strips overlap, this should not generate bias in your abundance estimates.  I showed this in a 2006 paper for point transect sampling.  When points were so close that each bird was expected to be detected from 3 or 4 poiints, bias was minimal.  So if there is a problem with your abundance estimates, there is probably another cause.

Steve Buckland

